📖 Surah Al-Qāri’ah (سورة القارعة) 

______________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________

Surah Number: 101
Type: Makki Surah
Total Ayat: 11
______________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________

🌟 Introduction

Ye surah “Al-Qāri’ah” ke naam se mashhoor hai, jiska matlab hai: dil ko hila dene wali, zor se takra dene wali cheez – yani Qayamat ka din.
Surah ka asal maqsad hai insaan ko aakhirat ke din ke manzar yaad dilana aur yeh batana ke insaan ki najat sirf uske aamaal ke tol par hogi.

______________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________

📝 Verse by Verse Tafseer

1. الْقَارِعَةُ

Al-Qāri’ah – “Qayamat ki zabardast pukarne wali cheez.”

Yahan sirf ek lafz se Allah ne Qayamat ka manzar saamne rakha.
Jaise koi aawaz jo dil ko jhatka de, jo insaan ko bechain kar de.

👉 Reflection: Duniya mein log Qayamat ko door samajhte hain, lekin Allah isse itna qareeb aur yaqeenan waqia hone wala dikhate hain ke sirf ek lafz hi kaafi hai.

______________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________

2. مَا الْقَارِعَةُ

“Qayamat kya hai?”

Sawal poocha gaya hai, taake insaan sochne lage ke akhir ye din kaisa hoga.

👉 Reflection: Jab Allah sawal karte hain, iska matlab hota hai ke insaan ko hila kar jagana hai.

______________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________

3. وَمَا أَدْرَاكَ مَا الْقَارِعَةُ

“Tu kya jaaney Qayamat kya hai?”

Yani insaan ki samajh mein bhi nahin aa sakta ke Qayamat ki dahshat kitni hogi.
Allah khud hi iska manzar bayan karte hain aage.

👉 Reflection: Hamari aqal bohot choti hai, akhirat ka manzar humari soch se bahar hai.

______________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________

4. يَوْمَ يَكُونُ النَّاسُ كَالْفَرَاشِ الْمَبْثُوثِ

“Us din log phaili hui titliyon ki tarah honge.”

Titliyan jalti hui roshni ke aas paas udti hain, idhar-udhar bhagti hain, koi tartib nahi hoti.
Qayamat ke din insaan bhi aise hi idhar-udhar bhag rahe honge – ghabrahat aur beqarari mein.

👉 Reflection: Aaj duniya mein insaan khud ko bohot taqatwar aur izzatdaar samajhta hai, lekin us din uski haalat ek titli ki tarah hogi – kamzor aur be-sahara.

______________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________

5. وَتَكُونُ الْجِبَالُ كَالْعِهْنِ الْمَنفُوشِ

“Pahaad ungdi hui oon ki tarah ho jaayenge.”

Pahaad jo duniya mein mazbooti ki nishani hain, us din bikhar kar udd jaayenge.
‘Ihnil-manfūsh ka matlab hai “rang-birangi ungdi hui oon” – yani asmaan mein udti hui rangin badal jaise.

👉 Reflection: Duniya mein jis cheez par insaan fakhr karta hai ke ye mazboot hai (jaise imaaratein, technology, science, resources), 
   wo sab Qayamat ke din bikhar kar khatam ho jaayega.

______________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________

6. فَأَمَّا مَن ثَقُلَتْ مَوَازِينُهُ

“Phir jis ka tarazu bhaari hoga (nekiyon se).”

Mizaan (tarazu) Qayamat ke din lagaya jaayega.
Har amal – chhota ho ya bada – us mein tola jaayega.
Bhaari mizaan = Zyada nek amal, imaan aur Allah ki raza.

👉 Reflection: Har nek amal ka wazan hai – chahe wo muskurana ho, kisi ko salam karna ho, ya zaruratmand ki madad karna ho.

______________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________

7. فَهُوَ فِي عِيشَةٍ رَّاضِيَةٍ

“To woh khushi aur sukoon wali zindagi mein hoga.”

Yani Jannat – jahan na gham hoga, na dukh, sirf Allah ki raza aur chain.

👉 Reflection: Aakhirat ki asli khushi Allah ki raza hai, duniya ki khushiyan sirf waqt ke liye hoti hain.

______________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________

8. وَأَمَّا مَنْ خَفَّتْ مَوَازِينُهُ

“Jiska tarazu halka hoga (neki kam, gunah zyada).”

Uske liye bara nuksan hai.
Matlab: sirf duniya ke liye jeena, akhirat bhool jaana.

👉 Reflection: Hamari sabse badi concern ye honi chahiye ke hamare nek amal kam toh nahi ho rahe?

______________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________

9. فَأُمُّهُ هَاوِيَةٌ

“To uska thikana Haawiyah hoga.”

“Umm” ka matlab hai asal ghar/jagah.
Yani uska ghar Haawiyah (Jahannum ka gaddha) hoga.

👉 Reflection: Jahannum insaan ka asli thikana ban jaaye – isse badi badnaseebi koi nahi.

______________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________

10. وَمَا أَدْرَاكَ مَا هِيَهْ

“Tu kya jaane Haawiyah kya hai?”

Allah dobara sawal karte hain – taake insaan ka dhyaan uske azaab ki taraf aur zyada ho.

👉 Reflection: Insaan ko har dafa yaad dilana padta hai, kyunke insaan bhoolne wala hai.

______________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________

11. نَارٌ حَامِيَةٌ

“Wo bohot hi garam aag hai.”

Garam ka matlab sirf garmi nahi, balke aisi aag jo insaan ko jala kar raakh kar degi.
Hamesha ki aag – na bujhne wali, na kam hone wali.

👉 Reflection: Duniya ki aag kuch seconds bhi bardasht nahi hoti, to akhirat ki aag kaisi hogi?

______________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________

🕌 Lessons for Us (Practical Takeaways)

Qayamat yaqeenan aayegi – isse bhoolna sabse badi ghalti hai.
Insaan ki najat sirf aur sirf uske aamaal par hai.
Chhoti nek amal ki ahmiyat hai – har nek amal tarazu mein wazan rakhta hai.
Duniya ki mazbooti (maal, taqat, rutba) kuch kaam nahi aayegi.
Har din apne aamaal ka hisaab lena chahiye – “Kya mera mizaan bhaari ho raha hai ya halka?”

______________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________

📌 Reflection 

“Agar aaj mera hisaab ho jaaye, to kya mera mizaan bhaari hoga ya halka?
Main apni roz ki zindagi mein kaunsi chhoti nek amal ko barha sakta hoon jisse mera tarazu mazboot ho?”


Noora, kya aa
